Upstream PR https://github.com/Mr-PauI/Walnut-CGB/pull/7 (MBC2 games could neither use nor save
their built-in RAM). Drop this file once the walnut-cgb submodule includes it.

From 9645d1343392c467f1254c84c608dd2220f5a128 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinko Korunic <dinko.korunic@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:29:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Keep MBC2 cartridge RAM enabled in gb_init

MBC2 has its 512x4-bit RAM built in, so MBC2 headers declare a RAM size
of 0. gb_init cleared cart_ram whenever num_ram_banks was 0, which made
the MBC2 RAM paths in __gb_read/__gb_write unreachable: MBC2 games could
neither use nor save their RAM. Exempt MBC2 from that check, as the note
further down in gb_init says num_ram_banks must be ignored for MBC2.
---
 walnut_cgb.h | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/walnut_cgb.h b/walnut_cgb.h
index 822511e..e5b5664 100644
--- a/walnut_cgb.h
+++ b/walnut_cgb.h
@@ -7692,8 +7692,9 @@ enum gb_init_error_e gb_init(struct gb_s *gb,
 	gb->num_ram_banks = num_ram_banks[gb_rom_read(gb, ram_size_location)];
 
 	/* If the ROM says that it support RAM, but has 0 RAM banks, then
-	 * disable RAM reads from the cartridge. */
-	if(gb->cart_ram == 0 || gb->num_ram_banks == 0)
+	 * disable RAM reads from the cartridge. MBC2 always reports 0 RAM
+	 * banks for its built-in RAM, so it is exempt. */
+	if(gb->cart_ram == 0 || (gb->num_ram_banks == 0 && gb->mbc != 2))
 	{
 		gb->cart_ram = 0;
 		gb->num_ram_banks = 0;
-- 
